#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Replace a legacy sandbox bootstrap after a proved whole-sandbox stop.

Private inventory: common project/env_file/runtime_image/docker_context and units
runner/keeper, plus sandbox:{name, clone_path, known_files, receipts_path,
script_path, profile_path, profile_source, systemd_user_dir, evidence_dir,
remote_ref, remote_name, declared_remote, declaration_files, release_image,
expected_sbx_version, legacy_dropins, legacy_command_markers, forbidden_values}.
Routes come ONLY from the explicit env file: FACTORY_GATEWAY_ADDRESS,
FORGE_TARGET_OWNER_URL, FORGE_SANDBOX_SIDECAR_URL, FORGE_SANDBOX_RUNNER_URL,
FLEET_MEMORY_SANDBOX_PORT (the sandbox's narrow memory door's gateway publish
port, as compose.yaml uses it; FLEET_MEMORY_PORT is the Dell's own tools' door),
MODEL_DOOR_PORT (the model door's gateway port, as compose.yaml uses it),
and GIT_DOOR_PORT when it is set (the Git door's gateway port, 17 October
2026; unset means no Git door rule, as before).
A sandbox entry may carry `slot` (1 to 19, one sandbox per project, 17 October
2026): it is then a project's own sandbox, whose env file must give it the
slot's ports (GIT_DOOR_PORT 31830+slot, FLEET_MEMORY_SANDBOX_PORT 31850+slot,
helper 8925+10*slot, runner 8924+10*slot) and whose rules may name on the
gateway only its own two doors, the model door, the answer service and the
embedder (never the bus or the model router).
An inventory may instead be {"sandboxes": [<inventory>, ...]}: one entry per
sandbox, each with its own project, env file and profile. --sandbox NAME picks
one; --plan without it plans every entry with its own files. The entries may
share no name, slot, clone, receipts folder, env file or door port, and an
entry without a slot (the shared legacy sandbox) gets no Git door port, in a
list or alone.
The producer profile retains all choices except gateway publish addresses,
explicit allow-rule replacements, receipts_path and cwd. sandbox.allow_replacements
maps old host:port entries to env variable NAMES holding replacement host:port.
No shell sourcing, ambient route overrides or broker clients.
"""
